{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"rg -n -A 22 -B 3 \\\"\\\\[requirement\\\\.SR-243\\\\]|\\\\[design\\\\.LLR-269\\\\]|\\\\[design\\\\.LLR-270\\\\]|\\\\[design\\\\.LLR-346\\\\]|\\\\[test\\\\.TC-265\\\\]|\\\\[test\\\\.TC-268\\\\]|\\\\[test\\\\.TC-384\\\\]|\\\\[test\\\\.TC-385\\\\]\\\" docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml docs/test/test-cases.toml\"","aggregated_output":"docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1931-phase = 6\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1932-aspect = \"process\"\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1933-\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml:1934:[requirement.SR-243]\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1935-title = \"Coordinator calls record sessions without committing outside claimed work\"\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1936-sn_refs = [\"SN-026\"]\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1937-boundary_refs = [\"B-10\"]\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1938-hat_refs = [\"UNATTENDED-OPS\", \"INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY\"]\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1939-requirement = \"When the coordinator's tooling launches a model session, the delivered coordinator call capability shall record the session in the usage record and, when the session starts outside a claimed unit of work, record its log without committing to the shared line of development.\"\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1940-rationale = \"A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-026 requires attributable routing among model families, and SR-222 requires a usage record for sessions the delivered loop launches, but neither reaches a coordinator-started session or states where its record may be committed. The unattended-operations lens identifies a partial or missing call record that leaves unattended progress unrecoverable, while the integrity-and-recoverability lens identifies telemetry committed to unrelated shared work as evidence with ambiguous provenance. Recording every coordinator session through the same usage record while retaining an out-of-work log without a shared commit was chosen over leaving coordinator sessions unrecorded or treating every checkout as a commit authority. Fed back to the need: its acceptance could state that every coordinator-started model session has attributable usage and a recoverable record without changing unrelated shared work. SR-231's rationale supplies the lane-local provenance lens; its adjudication-only boundary remains unchanged.\"\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1941-acceptance_criteria = \"For session-log recording, claimed work includes a linked worktree whose branch tree or the shared tree carries that branch's active work, including after the local claim has closed. A coordinator-started session in such claimed work records one usage record and its log commits with that work. A session started from the shared checkout, a detached checkout, or an unclaimed branch writes its log without a shared commit. A refused record commit is reported and is never success. A resumed authoring turn continues the recorded thread and refuses before launch when its relevant record is missing, damaged, foreign, or when an uncommitted relevant record is no older than it. The edit check distinguishes an edit from another call's standard record commit, reports edits, treats unreadable history as unable to check, and never reports a refused or unable check as success.\"\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1942-priority = \"S\"\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1943-verification = \"Test\"\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1944-status = \"Drafted\"\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1945-phase = 6\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml-1946-aspect = \"process\"\n--\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3044-component = \"CMP-008\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3045-phase = 6\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3046-\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:3047:[design.LLR-269]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3048-sr_refs = [\"SR-222\", \"SR-227\", \"SR-239\", \"SR-243\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3049-title = \"One session service launches and records every model call\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3050-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/session_service.py;project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py;project-trajectory/scripts/plan_runner.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3051-code_symbol = \"Call/_one_thread/_thread_argv/act/record/call/spool_dir/lane_branch/lane_wis/is_call_log;launch_session;_dp_session\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3052-detail = \"\"\"A role hands a Call its data (root, role, the route's template, model and prompt, provider, tier, route id, source event, attempt id, further attribution, env, deadlines, console renderer, attached) and nothing else. act builds the argv (agent_session.build_argv), lets the launched runner's adapter prepare it, launches it headless through run_session or attached through run_attached, reads the final text through the adapter, and fills the accounting: invocation id and timestamps, wall seconds, exit code and timeout kind, the adapter's usage record with usage-source and usage-status (known when input and output are both reported, partial when anything is, else unavailable), and the latest request's session id and context occupancy; a launch that raises is accounted with unavailable usage and re-raised. record writes one session log from the caller's row overlaid by that accounting, with the whole captured stream as its transcript, the raw stream to raw_dir/raw_name when given, and its own telemetry commit. call is act then record with the standard call_<invocation-id> row, recording an interrupted or failed launch too. The worker loop (launch_session, then record with the row it composed), the hands-on sitting, the route probe and the dual-plan hats (_dp_session) all launch through it; nothing else calls run_session, run_attached or the session-log writer. The service identity row accounts every call with session-mode, resumed only when its keep resumes a session, and keep-scope, the keep scope or empty; write_session_log records these as audit columns that no gate or scheduler reads. The record operation commits a log only from a claimed linked worktree, including a worktree whose branch claim has closed while the shared tree still carries its active work; from the shared checkout, a detached checkout, or an unclaimed branch, it writes the log to the primary checkout's spool and commits nothing. An unreadable claim read adds no claim; it spools only when neither readable tree establishes the linked worktree's claim. A spool write failure raises without a commit; a refused telemetry commit is reported to the caller; and a non-empty resumed thread identifier is refused with retained-session input before accounting. A non-empty unretained resume identifier records the resumed session mode without retaining that identifier. Standard call-log names remain distinct from gate-log names.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3053-rationale = \"\"\"A launch or logging path per role lets a fix to what a call records reach one path and miss the others. With one path, a role differs only in data, and a new provider difference goes to its adapter rather than into each role. The caller's row is overlaid rather than trusted, so what the service measured is never shadowed by a field a role composed.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3054-test_refs = \"(see TC-265)\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3055-status = \"Approved\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3056-component = \"CMP-008\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3057-phase = 6\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3058-\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:3059:[design.LLR-270]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3060-sr_refs = [\"SR-227\", \"SR-238\", \"SR-239\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3061-title = \"The keep operation retains adjudicator and loop reviewer sessions through act and record, inert at dial 0\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3062-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/session_keep.py;project-trajectory/scripts/session_service.py;project-trajectory/scripts/session_adapters.py;project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py;project-trajectory/scripts/dispatch.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/config.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3063-code_symbol = \"KeepConfig/keep_config/applies/FAMILY_RESET_CAP/GOVERNING_INPUT_FILES/GOVERNING_INPUT_GLOBS/primary_out_dir/store_lock/dir_lock/store_load/load_honoured/is_lease_only/store_remove/keep_release/APPLY_WAIT/_compaction_seen/_marker_name/keep_marker/publish_marker/Pending/_pending/_parse_marker/fold_marker/fold_markers/_released/_landing/Honoured/_folded/_busy/_observation/due_routes/retire_stale_lease/governing_hash/drain_reason/lineage/chain_pending/is_clear_point/retire_after_blackout/keep_for/keep_argv/keep_bookkeep/keep_abandon/keepwarm_due/_prepare_warm/_warm_candidates/_warm_keep/take_warm_lease/scoped_route/retire_scope/review_retention/ReviewRetention/_record_name/_read_record/_variant/_nonempty_str/_conforms;cli_version/plan_keep/KeepWarmer/KeepWarmer._ping/KeepWarmer._record_finished/KeepWarmer._raise_unended/KeepWarmer.finish/_pings_one_turn/_warm_routes/keep_warmer;ClaudeAdapter.mint/ClaudeAdapter.resume/ClaudeAdapter.one_turn/PlainAdapter.bounds_one_turn/CodexAdapter.resume/OpencodeAdapter.resume/reported_error/auth_failed;adjudication_keep/review_keep_scope/review_keep_templates/draw_session_route;run;reviewer_dials\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3064- detail = \"CONFIG. keep_config reads [adjudicator] (context_reset_pct 0..100, retain_for, keepwarm_minutes, reset_on_same_artifact); a missing table or an out-of-type value reads as that field's default. For ADJUDICATE calls, applies is true only for a retain_for brief on a named route with context_reset_pct above 0; otherwise plan_keep returns None before reading the runner version or the store, so at dial 0 nothing is minted, no resume flag is added, no store is written, the launch equals a fresh session's, and keep_warmer builds no warmer. For REVIEW-A or REVIEW-B calls, applies is true only on a named route with review_reset_pct above 0 and a non-empty scope; otherwise plan_keep returns None. For a covered call, plan_keep prepares the selected route through LLR-305 before keep_for, so a refusal takes no lease and creates no home; it passes the selected route id, prepared family and required Prepared launch to keep_for. STORE. primary_out_dir resolves the primary checkout's out/ directory from the git common directory; store_dir places one JSON record per route (IF-247) in its adjudicator child, so it outlives a lane worktree. dir_lock is the shared exclusive-file locking primitive for a named runtime-store directory; store_lock applies it to the adjudicator store. Every retained-session record write holds store_lock, a file created exclusively and stale after two minutes; a create of that file refused as access denied is read as the lock held and retried within the wait, a lock still held when the wait ends is refused as busy, naming an access refusal when that was the last, and another create refusal is raised after one attempt; each record is written through its own mkstemp file and os.replace. Every lease release, bookkeeping write and retirement is first published without the lock as one whole JSON store marker beside its record, named by the record stem and a hash of its publisher: a call's lease holder, or a fresh scope-retire id for scope retirement. A marker names the record identity, publisher, session id, generation, publication time and kind: bookkeep with the raw call observation, release, or retire with its reason. The publisher then applies its marker under store_lock within APPLY_WAIT, or it stands for the next locked read. A failed publication raises OSError and leaves no marker. A record carries a lease {holder, until}: keep_for takes it for the adjudication's wall deadline plus 300 s and, while another call holds the route's lease, waits up to lease_wait seconds before running 
